# Mode Study: A Lydian (repertoire plan: st-mode-lydian). An original 16-bar melody over a
# two-chord vamp: A (x02220) for two bars, then B (x24442) for two. D#, the raised fourth, is the
# colour of Lydian: a major scale with one note lifted, which gives it its floating, dreamy sound.
# A Lydian: A B C# D# E F# G#. The B major chord carries the D#.
# The melody lands on D# on a strong beat in bars 2, 3, 6, 8, 11, 12 and 15: over B it is the
# chord's third; over A (bars 2 and 6) it floats above the chord and then rises a half step to E.
# The last bars change faster (B in bar 15, A in bar 16) so the tune can come home to A.
# Fourth position, one finger per fret: finger 1 on fret 4 (D# on string 2, G# on string 1),
# finger 4 on fret 7. The same place on the neck as the Ionian study: only D becomes D#.
# The backing lets two strums a bar ring.
title: Mode Study: A Lydian
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the Lydian mode
